ent-a-u14-tile-floor-support = floor support
ent-a-u14-tile-applier-steel = steel floor
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-blue1-tile = steel support beam
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-blue1-tile-desc = A sturdy steel beam holding up the structure above. Destroying it brings down what it supports.
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-brown1-tile = wooden support beam
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-brown1-tile-desc = A wooden support beam. Cheap and weak; it will not take much punishment.
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-green1-tile = metal support beam
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-green1-tile-desc = A steel support beam. A solid, all-round support that takes a fair beating.
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-aqua1-tile = plasteel support beam
ent-a-u14-navalis-support-beam-aqua1-tile-desc = A plasteel support beam. The toughest support; it takes serious firepower to bring down.
ent-a-u14-rock-debris = rock debris
ent-a-u14-rock-debris-desc = A chunk of rock thrown loose by a cave-in.
ent-a-u14-structural-scanner = structural scanner
ent-a-u14-structural-scanner-desc = A handheld scanner that overlays the stability of dug-out ceilings. Toggle it in hand to see where a cavern is about to cave in.
ent-a-u14-z-stair-pure = z-level staircase
ent-a-u14-z-stair-pure-desc = A staircase connecting two z-levels. Walk onto it to traverse smoothly.
ent-a-u14-z-stair-frame-base = z-level staircase frame
ent-a-u14-z-stair-up = z-level stairs (up)
ent-a-u14-z-stair-up-desc = A staircase leading up one z-level. Lays a standing platform above with an open shaft and a support beam here.
ent-a-u14-z-stair-down = z-level stairs (down)
ent-a-u14-z-stair-down-desc = A stairwell leading down one z-level. Opens a shaft here, generates the level below, and places a return stair down there.
ent-a-u14-smelting-pot = smelting crucible
ent-a-u14-smelting-pot-desc = A squat iron crucible, its rim crusted with old slag. Ore comes out as metal, metal as plasteel, and a handful of ruined circuit boards as plastic - given a decent fire and the patience to sit by it.
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-camera-relay = spy camera relay
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-camera-relay-desc = A pocket relay that quietly ties the cell's spy cameras to their monitor. Keep it anywhere in range of both.
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-camera-monitor = CLF camera monitor
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-camera-monitor-desc = A patched-together handheld monitor wired into the cell's hidden spy cameras.
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-spy-camera = spy camera
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-spy-camera-desc = A tiny pinhole camera the cell can pocket, drop, or anchor to watch an approach and feed it back to their monitor.
ent-a-u14-spawn-point-c-l-f-sapper = Spawn Point CLF Sapper
ent-a-u14-a-package = a package
ent-a-u14-a-package-desc = A plain package with your name on it. Use it in hand to unpack your gear.
ent-a-u14-heavy-cell-kit = heavy cell kit
ent-a-u14-heavy-cell-kit-desc = The cell's deployable equipment, packed tight. Use it in hand to open the deploy menu and set out one piece at a time.
ent-a-u14-attachment-switch-desc = A tiny inverted sear chip that drops into a trigger group. Flip it on and the gun simply stops asking when to stop firing. Utterly illegal, wildly inaccurate, and prone to jamming.
ent-a-u14-sapper-workbench-kit = sapper's workbench kit
ent-a-u14-sapper-workbench-kit-desc = A folded field workbench. Use it in hand to unfold it where you stand. Only a trained sapper knows how.
ent-a-u14-sapper-workbench = sapper's workbench
ent-a-u14-sapper-workbench-desc = This workbench seems designed with weapon grips, detailed computer components, and specialized device parts in mind. Feed it sheets of metal, plasteel, plastic, or wood; lay looted parts on top for the fancier recipes.
ent-a-u14-sapper-siphon-rig = siphon rig
ent-a-u14-sapper-siphon-rig-desc = A skimming rig of scavenged wiring and cloned card readers. Clamp it onto a colony ATM, budget console, or ASRS terminal and it quietly bleeds the funds out into cash.
ent-a-u14-sapper-i-e-d = buried IED
ent-a-u14-sapper-i-e-d-desc = An improvised explosive device buried under the surface, wired to a hidden pressure plate. It packs enough charge to level whatever unlucky enough to stand on it.
ent-a-u14-sapper-shotgun-trap = shotgun trap
ent-a-u14-sapper-shotgun-trap-desc = A sawn-off barrel lashed to a stake and rigged to a tripline. Step in front and it empties a shell of buckshot into your legs.
ent-a-u14-sapper-tripwire-trap = tripwire charge
ent-a-u14-sapper-tripwire-trap-desc = A firing box wired to a near-invisible tripline that runs a few tiles ahead to a stake. Attach grenades or explosives to the box, then plant it - anything that isn't a friendly crossing the wire sets it all off at once. Cut it with wirecutters to make it safe.
ent-a-u14-sapper-tripwire-end-placer = tripwire spool
ent-a-u14-sapper-tripwire-end-placer-desc = The loose end of a tripline, trailing wire back to a planted charge. Use it where you want the line to end.
ent-a-u14-sapper-tripwire-segment-desc = A near-invisible wire strung taut between a charge and its stake. Crossing it is a very bad idea.
ent-a-u14-sapper-tripwire-end = tripwire stake
ent-a-u14-sapper-tripwire-end-desc = The far stake a tripline is tied off to.
ent-a-u14-sapper-snare-trap = snare trap
ent-a-u14-sapper-snare-trap-desc = A hidden tangle of wire and hooks. Step in it and it whips tight, binding your hands and yanking you off your feet.
ent-a-u14-sapper-crafting-kit = improvised trap materials
ent-a-u14-sapper-crafting-kit-desc = A bundle of scrap, wire, and scavenged explosives. Use it in hand to fabricate CLF traps wherever you stand.
ent-a-u14-sapper-trap-toolbox = sapper trap kit
ent-a-u14-sapper-trap-toolbox-desc = A battered toolbox packed with improvised charges and triplines. Everything a CLF sapper needs to seed a killbox.
ent-a-u14-sapper-trap-area-preview = trap coverage
ent-a-u14-sapper-trap-area-preview-desc = Where the trap being set will trigger.
ent-a-u14-sapper-audio-trap = audio trap
ent-a-u14-sapper-audio-trap-desc = A whistle alarm wired to a near-invisible tripline. Anything crossing the wire sets off a shrill blast and radios the cell where it happened. Cut it with wirecutters to silence it.
ent-xeno-collapse-resin = scab resin
ent-xeno-collapse-resin-desc = A dark crust of hardened resin, spun thick across a hole in the floor. It holds weight, barely.
ent-a-u14-govfor-computer-dropship-weapons-small = dropship weapons computer
ent-a-u14-govfor-computer-dropship-weapons-small-desc = A compact computer that can manage equipment, weapons and simulations installed on the dropship.
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-home = dropship destination(home)
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-home-desc = Defines a valid location for the dropships to FTL to when piloted. (home)
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-opfor-whitelist = dropship destination
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-opfor-whitelist-desc = Defines a valid location for the dropships to FTL to when piloted.
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-third-party-whitelist = dropship destination (third party)
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-third-party-whitelist-desc = Defines a valid location for third party dropships to FTL to when piloted.
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-third-party-return = Return to Deep Space
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-third-party-return-desc = Sends a third party dropship back to its holding pattern.
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-govfor-whitelist = dropship destination (govfor)
ent-c-m-dropship-destination-govfor-whitelist-desc = Defines a valid location for government dropships to FTL to when piloted.
ent-a-u14-govfor-computer-dropship-pilot-small = dropship navigation computer
ent-a-u14-govfor-computer-dropship-pilot-small-desc = A compact computer that can pilot the dropship and designate tactical landings.
ent-c-m-computer-dropship-navigation-third-party = dropship navigation computer (Third Party)
ent-r-m-c-c-l-f-cell-leader-armband = CLF cell leader armband
ent-r-m-c-c-l-f-cell-leader-armband-desc = A crudely sewn armband. It's dyed in the colors of the Colonial Liberation Front.
ent-r-m-c-coat-pa-p = PaP uniform jacket
ent-r-m-c-coat-pa-p-desc = A People's Armed Police service jacket featuring small dispersed para-aramid inserts providing the barest of defensive functionality, and a Personal Light Unit rig.
ent-r-m-c-jumpsuit-s-p-p-pa-p = PaP service uniform
ent-r-m-c-jumpsuit-s-p-p-pa-p-desc = A pair of blue-grey slacks coupled with a blue shirt, featuring venlar armor inserts at critical areas to protect from blades and low caliber ballistics.
ent-r-m-c-synth-reset-key-seegson = Seegson Working Joe reboot key
ent-r-m-c-synth-reset-key-seegson-desc = A rugged reboot key designed for Seegson Working Joe synthetic units. It must be recharged after use.
ent-r-m-c-synth-reset-key-hyperdyne = Hyperdyne synthetic reset key
ent-r-m-c-synth-reset-key-hyperdyne-desc = An independent Hyperdyne-pattern reset key for rebooting synthetic units after critical failure. It must be recharged after use.
ent-r-m-c-glasses-security-swat = tactical SWAT HUD
ent-r-m-c-glasses-security-swat-desc = Flash-resistant goggles with inbuilt combat and security information.
ent-c-m-glasses-m96-c-sight = M96C special operations sight
ent-c-m-glasses-m96-c-sight-desc = A specialized variation of the M96 scout sight system, intended for use with the high-power M96C anti-tank sniper rifle. Allows for highlighted imaging of surroundings, as well as detection of thermal signatures even from a great distance.
ent-r-m-c-glasses-m4-s-p-r-battle-sight-r-c-m = Royal Crown Marine marksman's goggles
ent-r-m-c-glasses-m4-s-p-r-battle-sight-r-c-m-desc = A headset and night vision goggles system used by RMC Marksmen. Allows highlighted imaging of surroundings.
