ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-cupola-tracer = cupola cannon ammo crate (tracer)
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-cupola-tracer-desc = Tracer ammunition for cupola-mounted vehicle cannons. Burns bright in flight to help the gunner walk fire onto target, at the cost of giving away the tank's position.
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-a-p-f-s-d-s = LTB APFSDS cannon shell
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-a-p-f-s-d-s-desc = Ammunition for light tank cannons. A fin-stabilized discarding-sabot penetrator with no explosive filler, meant to punch through armor rather than fragment. Barely scratches infantry or structures.
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-h-e-a-t = LTB HEAT cannon shell
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-h-e-a-t-desc = Ammunition for light tank cannons. A shaped-charge warhead that punches a focused jet through armor with a small blast, backed by light fragmentation. Less effective against armor than a dedicated penetrator, but hits far harder than a standard HE shell.
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-h-e = LTB HE cannon shell
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-h-e-desc = Ammunition for light tank cannons. A thin-walled high-explosive shell that trades armor penetration for a much wider blast and fragmentation radius.
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-canister = LTB canister cannon shell
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-canister-desc = Ammunition for light tank cannons. A short-ranged anti-personnel round packed with metal shot that bursts into a lethal spray shortly after firing. Nearly useless against armor.
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-napalm = LTB napalm cannon shell
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-l-t-b-cannon-napalm-desc = Ammunition for light tank cannons. A napalm-filled shell with very little blast, but scatters sticky burning fragments that spread across the impact area. Good for burning out entrenched positions or setting the field alight.
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-grenade-launcher-h-e-f-a = grenade launcher ammo crate (HEFA)
ent-c-m-u-ammo-box-grenade-launcher-h-e-f-a-desc = Ammunition for vehicle grenade launchers. 30mm HEFA grenades, a fragmentation round that showers the area in shrapnel. Better against infantry, weaker against structures and vehicles than HEDP.
