ent-c-m-u-pipe-bomb = pipe bomb
ent-c-m-u-pipe-bomb-desc = A cheap way to injure someone. Designed by your local insurgent’s.
ent-c-m-u-pipe-bomb-fuse = pipe bomb
ent-c-m-u-pipe-bomb-fuse-desc = Incomplete. Seems like it need’s Cable as the fuse
ent-c-m-u-pipe-bomb-casing = pipe bomb
ent-c-m-u-pipe-bomb-casing-desc = Empty casing. Seems like it need a Lighter.
ent-c-m-u14-tear-gas-grenade = M19-NL gas grenade
ent-c-m-u14-tear-gas-grenade-desc = Sometimes referred to as the "Fogger", the M19 nonlethal gas grenade was intended for boarding actions against pirate vessels or putting down civil unrest, saturating spaces with an irritating aerosol with temporary neuromuscular effects.
ent-a-u14-tele-baton = telescopic baton
ent-a-u14-tele-baton-desc = A telescopic baton for incapacitating people with.
ent-a-u14-tool-pickaxe-desc = Great for introducing rocks to gravity and heavy enough to convince even the toughest stone to move aside.
ent-a-u14-tool-machete-desc = Chop a path through dense jungles and thick vegetation with this brutal blade. A favorite for marines and warlords alike.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m-a-r40-tactical-desc = A cheap, reliable assault rifle chambered in 7.62x39mm. Commonly found in the hands of criminals or mercenaries, or in the hands of the UPP or CLF. This one has been equipped with an after-market ammo-counter.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m41-a-m-k2-tactical = Magazine
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m16-a2 = M16A2 rifle
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m16-a2-desc = An old, reliable design first adopted by the U.S. military in the 1980s. Something like this belongs in a museum of war history. It is chambered in 5.56x45mm.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m16-a2-larue = M16A2 Larue rifle
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m16-a2-larue-desc = An 'improved' pattern of M16A2 recently released on the civilian market, proclaiming it is 'cutting edge modularity and optics friendliness on a budget' It met limited success in it's intended market It has seen stable but small sales regardless.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-a-r10 = AR10 rifle
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-a-r10-desc = An old, reliable design. Something like this belongs in a museum of war history. It is chambered in 5.56x45mm.
ent-c-m-u-magazine-rifle-m16-extended = M16 Extended Magazine (5.56x45mm)
ent-c-m-u-magazine-rifle-m16-extended-desc = A 30-round 5.56x45mm magazine developed in the early 1970s for the M16 series rifles.
ent-a-u14-magazine-rifle-m41-a-e2 = M41AE2 AP magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-two-bore = Double-Deuce Two-Bore Rifle
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-two-bore-desc = A Custom-Built Twin-Barreled Two-Bore Guage Rifle. Built to hunt the largest - or most dangerous - of game. She's Forty-Five Pounds Dry, Illegal in three Sectors, and on a hair-trigger. Take care of her, and she'll take care of you - and anything you point her at.
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-two-bore = Rifle Cartridge (Two-Bore)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-two-bore-desc = A Two-Bore rifle cartridge. This round makes a .50 Cal look like a pea-shooter. Pray you never get hit with this thing.
ent-a-u14-attachment-two-bore-stock = Two Bore Rifle solid stock
ent-a-u14-attachment-two-bore-stock-desc = Integrated into the Two Bore Rifle. You shouldn't have this.
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-r-x-f-m5 = RXF-M5 EVA Laser Pistol
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-r-x-f-m5-desc = A High power focusing laser pistol with an internal nuclear battery, designed for Extra-Vehicular Activity. Though it works just about anywhere really. Deprived from the same technology as laser welders. Issued by the Weyland-Yutani Corportation, but also available on the civilian market.
ent-a-u14-magazine-mar50-l-m-g-a-p = MAR AP drum magazine (7.62x39mm)
ent-a-u14-magazine-mar50-l-m-g-a-p-desc = A 7.62x39mm drum magazine for the MAR-50 LMG.
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-m-a-r40-a-p = Cartridge (7.62x39mm AP)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-m-a-r40-a-p-desc = A 7.62x39mm AP rifle cartridge
ent-a-u14-case-motion-detector-r-m-c = RMC motion detectors case
ent-a-u14-case-motion-detector-r-m-c-desc = A case containing four individual handheld motion detectors programmed to operate with RMC IFF.
ent-a-u14-gun-case-pistol-l165-a1 = L165A1 pistol case
ent-a-u14-gun-case-pistol-l165-a1-desc = A gun case containing the L165A1. Comes with two magazines.
ent-a-u14-box-magazine-pistol-l165-a1-empty = magazine box (L165A1 x 16)
ent-a-u14-ballistic-shield-r-m-c = FBS-B ballistic shield
ent-a-u14-ballistic-shield-r-m-c-desc = Ballistic shield used by the royal marines commando. This shield is commonly used during boarding actions due to its lightweight but durable design. Does not help against explosives.
ent-a-u14-l64-a3-sniper-rifle-desc = A lightweight designated marksman rifle developed by Howatomo Precision Machining for the Royal Marines. Designed to provide commandos with responsive long range reach past what the old L90 could manage. A continuous-charge HESH payload removes the requirement for traditional armor piercing steel core ammunition, and improves damage retention at extended range. Faster cycle rate of the breech and a light trigger gives fast and precise followup shots even at thousand meter distances.
ent-a-u14-magazine-sniper-l64-a3 = L64A3 squash-head magazine (8.88x51mm)
ent-a-u14-magazine-sniper-l64-a3-desc = A magazine of L10A7 squash-head match-grade 8.88x51mm ammo.
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-l64-a3-squashhead = L10A7 Squash-head Cartridge (8.88x51mm)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-l64-a3-squashhead-desc = A 8.88x51mm Squash-head rifle cartridge
ent-a-u14-mortar-kit-r-m-c = L53A1 light mortar portable kit
ent-a-u14-mortar-kit-r-m-c-desc = A manual, crew-operated light mortar system intended to provide mobile fire support for a troop of Royal Marines. Needs to be set down first.
ent-a-u14-base-air-burst-grenade-r-m-c = 20-mm air burst grenade
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l103-a1 = L103A1 20mm HE grenade
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l103-a1-desc = A 20mm grenade that explodes upon impact. Less powerful than full-sized grenades.
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l108-a1 = L108A1 20mm HESH grenade
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l108-a1-desc = High-Explosive Dual-Purpose. A small, but deceptively strong blast grenade that has been phasing out the M15 HE grenades alongside the 30mm HEFA. Capable of being loaded in grenade launchers, or thrown by hand.
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l101-a2 = L101A2 20mm nerve-agent grenade
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l101-a2-desc = A 20mm grenade that explodes into a voluminous cloud of nerve gas upon impact.
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l104-a1 = L104A1 20mm fragmentation grenade
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l104-a1-desc = A 20mm grenade that explodes into shrapnel upon impact.
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l103-a1-i = L103A1/I 20mm incendiary grenade
ent-a-u1420-m-m-grenade-l103-a1-i-desc = A 20mm grenade that explodes into flaming shrapnel & a pool of incendiary compound upon impact.
ent-a-u14-hornet-shell-l104-a1-h = L104A1/H 20mm holo-targetting grenade
ent-a-u14-hornet-shell-l104-a1-h-desc = A 20mm grenade that explodes into shrapnel upon impact. The shrapenl of this one douses the target in a chemical compound which aids in target acquisition by sensors.
ent-a-u14-air-burst-projectile-frag-r-m-c = L104A1 20mm grenade
ent-a-u14-air-burst-projectile-incendiary-r-m-c = L103A1/I 20mm grenade
ent-a-u14-air-burst-projectile-hornet-r-m-c = L104A1/H 20mm grenade
ent-a-u14-shrapnel-jagged-r-m-c = jagged shrapnel
