ent-a-u14-weapon-launcher-l164-a3 = L164A3 multi-shot grenade launcher
ent-a-u14-weapon-launcher-l164-a3-desc = A lightweight support weapon fielded by the Royal Marines. Chambered in small 20mm grenades, it lacks the punch of larger bore grenade launchers, but makes up for that in rate of fire.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifleprodigyrifle-a-r-desc = The Modular Combat System Mark X Pulse Rifle, or MCS-X Pulse Rifle for short, is the standard weapon used by the prodigy security forces employed by Prodigy Corporation. The weapon has a bullpup design, intended for use in cramped urban environments. The MCS-X features a digital ammunition counter, and is capable of holding ninety-five rounds.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifleprodigyrifle-magazine-standard = MCS-X Pulse Rifle magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifleprodigyrifle-magazine-a-p = MCS-X Pulse Rifle AP magazine (10x24mm)
ent-c-m-u14-weapon-pistol-glock75-desc = Austrian legend, designed in XX century, Glock quickly became a major player on the pistol market. This version was produced on a license for Prodigy CORP for security and police forces, features an underbarrel rail for a taser.
ent-c-m-u14-weapon-pistol-glock77-desc = Austrian legend, designed in XX century, Glock quickly became a major player on the pistol market. This version was produced on a license for Prodigy CORP for security and police forces, features an underbarrel rail for a taser and fully automatic mode.
