ent-a-u14-packet-grenade-high-explosive-u-p-p-desc = It contains six Type 6 fragmentation grenades. Handle with care.
ent-a-u14-box-h-e-d-p-u-p-p = Type 6 fragmentation grenade box
ent-a-u14-box-h-e-d-p-u-p-p-desc = A secure box holding 12 type 6 fragmentation grenades. Ensure pins are in place before removing from the box.
ent-a-u14-packet-grenade-smoke-u-p-p = RDG-17 smoke grenade packet
ent-a-u14-packet-grenade-smoke-u-p-p-desc = It contains six RDG-17 smoke grenades.
ent-a-u14-box-smoke-u-p-p = RDG-17 smoke grenade box
ent-a-u14-box-smoke-u-p-p-desc = A secure box holding 12 RDG-17 smoke grenades. Ensure pins are in place before removing from the box.
ent-a-u14-packet-grenade-incendiary-u-p-p = Type 8 incendiary grenade packet
ent-a-u14-packet-grenade-incendiary-u-p-p-desc = It contains three type 8 white phosphorus grenades.
ent-a-u14-box-h-i-d-p-u-p-p = Type 8 WP grenade box
ent-a-u14-box-h-i-d-p-u-p-p-desc = A secure box holding 12 type 8 WP grenades. Ensure pins are in place before removing from the box.
ent-a-u-weapon-rifle-m75-a-m-a-s-desc = The M75A MAS is Armat Battlefield Systems newest modular weapons platform, intended to replace the aging M41 MK1 Pulse Rifle. The weapon is still in limited field testing among select CCAF infantry units.
ent-a-u14-magazine-rifle-m75-a-m-a-s = M75AMAS Magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-m75-a-m-a-s = Cartridge (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-m75-a-m-a-s-desc = A 10x24mm rifle cartridge
ent-a-u-weapon-rifle-c10-a6-b-r-desc = A reflexive burst rifle designed for the CCAF by Armat Battlefield Systems. It delivers a fast three round burst upon trigger pull, all fired before the operator perceives recoil. The weapon is still in limited field testing among select CCAF infantry units.
ent-a-u14-magazine-rifle-c10-a6-b-r = C10A6BR Magazine (.25 ACP)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-c10-a6-b-r = Cartridge (.25 ACP)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-c10-a6-b-r-desc = A .25 ACP pistol cartridge
ent-a-u-weapon-rifle-m100-m-g-r-desc = An airburst grenade launcher platform designed for CCAF section grenadiers, replacing the M41As underslung launcher. It fires mag-fed 40mm airburst grenades. This weapon is equipped with IFF and is still in limited field testing among select CCAF infantry units.
ent-a-u14-magazine-rifle-m100-m-g-r = M100MGR Magazine (40mm)
ent-a-u-weapon-rifle-m20-a-desc = More commonly known as the Harrington Rifle, a past designation of the USCMC and the phased out predecessor of the M41A Pulse Rifle. More commonly seen in the hands of territorial guard or in colony armories for emergencies.
ent-a-u14-magazine-rifle-m20-a = M20a Magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-m20-a = Cartridge (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-cartridge-rifle-m20-a-desc = A 10x24mm rifle cartridge
ent-a-u14-attachment-m20-a-underbarrel-shotgun = M20A underbarrel shotgun
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-f44-a-a-desc = F44AA is an electronic pulse-action assault rifle. Manufactured by the Weyland-Yutani, the rifle is equipped with an amining assist computer and safety.
ent-a-u14-magazine-rifle-f44-a-a = F44AA magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-attachment-f44-a-a-stock-collapsible = F44AA folding stock
ent-a-u14-attachment-f44-a-a-stock-collapsible-desc = The standard back end of any gun starting with F44AA.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-x-m4-r-a-desc = The XM4RA carbine is being developed for the United States Colonial Marines Corps as a part of Special Operations Peculiar Carbine (SOPCAR). Originally started as a weapon for the Marine Raiders, this carbine became a prototype for a new generation self defense weapon for tank crews and Marine Secuity Guard.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-x-m4-r-a1 = XM4RA1 carbine
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-x-m4-r-a1-desc = The XM4RA1 carbine is a part of Special Operations Peculiar Carbine (SOPCAR). Originally started as a weapon for the Marine Raiders, this carbine became a prototype for a new generation self defense weapon for tank crews and Marine Secuity Guard. This modification has full-auto firemode.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-x-m4-r-a1-s-o-p-m-o-d = XM4RA1 SOPMOD carbine
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-x-m4-r-a1-s-o-p-m-o-d-desc = The XM4RA1 SOPMOD carbine is a part of new self-defense and special operations program for USCMC. Specifically SOPMOD modification is being developed for Marine Raiders needs.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m49-a-desc = An early modification of the M49A marksman rifle, the A2 has a tweaked gas-system and fire-control-group, giving it better cyclic rate and a two round burst-fire mode. Fielded almost exclusively by FORECON units in the USCM. This one is painted in a fresh coat of the newer Humbrol 76 camouflage.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m41-a-m-k1-recon-suppressed = M41A pulse rifle MK1
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-m41-a-m-k1-recon-suppressed-desc = Pulse action 10x24mm caseless assault rifle of the USCMC, personal friend of any Marine. This one is painted in a fresh coat of the newer Humbrol 76 camouflage and is used by Force Reconnaissance & MARSOC units.
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-m4-a4-desc = A redesigned version of the M4A3 Service Pistol. The M4A4 was developed by ARMAT to be the next generation of service handgun used by US forces. However, due to limited budget constraints, the M4A4 has yet to see widespread adoption among the USCM and has mainly been issued to the US Army and Aerospace Force. This weapon uses M4A3 magazines.
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-m4-a4-empty = Magazine
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-m48-a4-desc = A timeless classic since the first World War, the M1911A1 has limited use with the USCM, and is often used as a sidearm by non-governmental bodies due to its reliability. This is a modernized version with an ammo counter and a polymer grip, designated M48A4. Chambered in .45 ACP.
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-m48-a4-empty = Magazine
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-m48-a4-tactical = SOCOM M48A4 service pistol
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-m48-a5-officer-desc = A timeless classic since the first World War, the M1911A1 has limited use with the USCM, and is often used as a sidearm by non-governmental bodies due to its reliability. An adaptation of the M48A4, with a reinforced chamber, barrel and slide to handle higher pressure loads, designated the M48A5. Chambered in .45 Super, but can load normal .45 ACP also.
ent-a-u14-magazine-pistol-m48-a4 = M48A4 magazine (.45)
ent-a-u14-magazine-pistol-m48-a5-super = M48A5 Super magazine (.45 Super)
ent-a-u14-magazine-pistol-m48-a5-super-desc = A .45 Automagnum Super pistol magazine for the M48A5.
ent-a-u14-cartridge-pistol-m48-a5-super = cartridge (.45 Super)
ent-a-u14-bullet-pistol45-super = bullet (.45 Super)
ent-a-u14-weapon-x-m99-a = XM99A phased plasma pulse rifle
ent-a-u14-weapon-x-m99-a-desc = An experimental directed energy weapon system designed by Armat, the XM99A is a long-range prototype rifle that fires super-heated blasts of plasma. The XM99A will slowly recharge its lithium battery drum over time using static electricity.
ent-a-u14-plasma-shot = plasma pulse ray
ent-a-u14-case-x-m99-a = XM99A phased plasma pulse rifle case
ent-a-u14-case-x-m99-a-desc = A large case for storing an phased plasma pulse rifle, an experimental directed energy weapon system designed by Armat
ent-a-u14-m-k86-mount = mk86 automatic grenade launcher
ent-a-u14-m-k86-mount-desc = The disassembled Mk86 AGL, with its telescopic tripods folded up and unable to fire.
ent-a-u14-a-g-l-m-k86-desc = The top half of a Mk86 AGL. However it ain't much use without a tripod.
ent-a-u14-magazine-mk86-frag = Mk86 Ammunition Box (AGM-F 40mm frag grenade)
ent-a-u14-magazine-mk86-frag-desc = A box of 15, AGM-F 40mm frag grenade rounds for the mk86 automatic grenade launcher system.
ent-a-u14-magazine-mk86-hornet = Mk86 Ammunition Box (AGM-H 40mm hornet grenade)
ent-a-u14-magazine-mk86-hornet-desc = A box of 15, AGM-H 40mm hornet grenade rounds for the mk86 automatic grenade launcher system.
ent-a-u14-magazine-mk86-smoke = Mk86 Ammunition Box (AGM-S 40mm smoke grenade)
ent-a-u14-magazine-mk86-smoke-desc = A box of 15, AGM-S 40mm smoke grenade rounds for the mk86 automatic grenade launcher system.
ent-a-u14-mk86-case = Mk86 automatic grenade launcher case
ent-a-u14-mk86-case-desc = A gun case containing the Mk86 automatic grenade launcher. Comes with 5 magazines
ent-a-u14-weapon-sniper-rifle-m42-a2-desc = The M42A2 designated marksman rifle is currently used by the LACN landing forces, originally supposed to be mass produced for the USCM until it lost his place against the M4RA due to its superior magazine capacity, longer barrel and superior modularity. the M42A2 still was a pretty decent option due to its lower production cost and more compact figure that lead to it getting adopted by both the LACN Landing Forces and Naval Commandos. the Commandos specially using it in larger numbers due to how reliable and easy to maintain it was during deep infiltration operations. This rifle takes M42A magazines.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-kramer-a-r-desc = Alternately referred to as the Kramer or KAR, it is an automatic assault rifle manufactured by Kramer Metallarbeiten GmbH and is used by many military forces across the United Americas.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-kramer-magazine-standard = Kramer magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-kramer-magazine-a-p = Kramer AP magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-t-p-r23-b-desc = A modernized variant of the M4A3 Service Pistol. The TPR23B was developed as part of a cost saving initiative by the LACN. Instead of acquiring new sidearms like the USCM, the LACN opted to retrofit existing M4A3 stocks with massproduced upgrade kits. This weapon takes M4A3 magazines.
ent-a-u14-weapon-pistol-t-p-r23-b-empty = Magazine
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-kramer-l-s-w-desc = Also referred to as the Kramer or KAR, the Kramer Light Support Weapon is an automatic squad support variant of the standard Kramer assault rifle. Manufactured by Kramer Metallarbeiten GmbH, the KAR sees widespread use across United Americas.
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-kramer-magazine-l-s-w-standard = Kramer LSW box magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-weapon-rifle-kramer-magazine-l-s-w-a-p = Kramer LSW AP box magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-weapon-s-m-g-x-m-p5-a6-h-a-z-o-p-s-desc = Winner of the 2172 HAZOPS Close Quarters Weapon program, this German-based "SMG" answers the question; "What if we put the standard USCMC rifle caliber in a machinepistol?". Despite low accuracy, it has a high firerate and impressive stopping power. Chambered in 10x24mm. Can load M41A magazines.
ent-a-u14-attachment-m203-a4-grenade-launcher = M203A4 grenade launcher
ent-a-u14-attachment-m203-a4-grenade-launcher-desc = A weapon-mounted, reloadable grenade launcher.
ent-a-u14-magazine-x-m-p5-a6 = XMP5A6 magazine (10x24mm)
ent-a-u14-magazine-x-m-p5-a6-desc = What have they done with my bannana clip? Uses 10x24mm.
ent-a-u14-weapon-shotgun-s-p-a-s12-h-a-z-o-p-s = SPAS-12-HAZ
ent-a-u14-weapon-shotgun-s-p-a-s12-h-a-z-o-p-s-desc = Designed for HAZOPS teams, this cut-down SPAS-12 looks mostly the same as old Earth models, but the internal workings are completely rebuilt, allowing for a devasting "triple-shot" mode.
ent-a-u14-weapon-flamer-m240-a2-h-a-z-o-p-s-desc = The USCMC's answer to WY's Flammerwerfer 3. Much more effective than the standard M240, but inflicts a movement penality. Typically issued to HAZOPS.
ent-a-u14-tank-flamer-m240-a2-h-a-z-o-p-s = M240A2 heavy incinerator tank
ent-a-u14-tank-flamer-m240-a2-h-a-z-o-p-s-desc = A heavy, high capacity tank utilized by the M240A2. Has a colorless HAZOPS logo imprinted on the side.
ent-a-u14-tank-flamer-m240-a2-h-a-z-o-p-s-napalm-b = M240A2 heavy incinerator tank (B)
ent-a-u14-tank-flamer-m240-a2-h-a-z-o-p-s-napalm-b-desc = A heavy, high capacity tank utilized by the M240A2. Has a colorless HAZOPS logo imprinted on the side. This one seems to contain 'Napalm-B'
ent-a-u14-tank-flamer-m240-a2-h-a-z-o-p-s-napalm-x = M240A2 heavy incinerator tank (X)
