ent-a-u14-armor-smart-gun-u-n-i-s-c-combat-harness = M56 UNISC Combat Harness
ent-a-u14-armor-smart-gun-u-n-i-s-c-combat-harness-desc = An M56 Combat Harness specially made for Smartgunners.
ent-a-u14-u-n-i-s-c-m10-helmet = UNISC M10 Helmet
ent-a-u14-u-n-i-s-c-m10-helmet-desc = Standard Issue Helmet used by UNISC. Provides modest protection from bullet and melee attacks at the head. It also has an inbuilt camera allowing for command staff to observe the squad's actions.
ent-a-u14-u-n-i-s-c-m11-helmet = UNISC M11 Helmet
ent-a-u14-u-n-i-s-c-m11-helmet-desc = A slightly fancier helmet for UNISC leadership. This one contains a small built-in camera and has cushioning to project your fragile brain.
ent-a-u14-u-n-i-s-c-fatigues = UNISC fatigues
ent-a-u14-u-n-i-s-c-fatigues-desc = Standard-issue UNISC fatigues. They have shards of light Kevlar to help protect against stabbing weapons and bullets.
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-armor = ISAS Armor
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-armor-desc = Standard body armor worn by frontline CCAF infantry. This unit has been modified for compatibility with the Integrated Soldier Armor System backpack, which links to a CG982 ISACV to deliver real time combat data. Currently in field trials with select CCAF infantry units.
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-armor-padless = ISAS Padless Armor
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-armor-padless-desc = Standard body armor worn by frontline CCAF infantry. This unit has been modified for compatibility with the Integrated Soldier Armor System backpack, which links to a CG982 ISACV to deliver real time combat data. Currently in field trials with select CCAF infantry units. This unit has had its shoulder pads removed.
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-armor-stripped = ISAS Stripped Armor
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-armor-stripped-desc = Standard body armor worn by frontline CCAF infantry. This unit has been modified for compatibility with the Integrated Soldier Armor System backpack, which links to a CG982 ISACV to deliver real time combat data. Currently in field trials with select CCAF infantry units. This unit has had its shoulder pads and greaves removed.
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-helmet-i-s-a-c-v = CG982 ISACV
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-helmet-i-s-a-c-v-desc = Standard Issue Helmet used by the CCAF. This variant is fitted with an experimental Improved Situational Awareness Combat Visor. Currently undergoing field trials with select CCAF infantry units.
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-uniform = CCAF Fatigues
ent-a-u14-c-c-a-f-uniform-desc = Standard-issue Canadian Colonial Armed Forces fatigues. They have shards of light Kevlar to help protect against stabbing weapons and bullets.
ent-a-u14-belt-marine-u-p-p = Type 41 pattern ammo load rig
ent-a-u14-belt-marine-u-p-p-desc = The Type 41 load rig is the standard-issue load-bearing equipment of the UPP military. The primary function of this belt is to provide easy access to mags for the Type 71 during operations. Despite being designed for the Type 71 weapon system, the pouches are modular enough to fit other types of ammo and equipment.
ent-a-u14-belt-marine-army-u-p-p = 6B80 pattern ammo rig
ent-a-u14-belt-marine-army-u-p-p-desc = The 6B80 is an outdated but reliable ammo rig, formerly standard for the UPP Army. Its modular belt holds various munitions, still used by UPP security forces and reserves for its rugged design.
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-general-u-p-p = Type 48-M general utility pouch
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-general-u-p-p-desc = A small, lightweight pouch that can be clipped onto U-pattern UPP armor to provide additional storage. The newer 48-M model, while uncomfortable, can also be clipped around the waist.
ent-a-u14-belt-medical-u-p-p = Type 41 pattern medical storage rig
ent-a-u14-belt-medical-u-p-p-desc = The Type 41 is the standard load-bearing equipment of UPP military. It consists of a modular belt with various clips. This version is a less common configuration, designed to transport medical supplies. \nRight click its sprite and click \"toggle belt mode\" to take pills out of bottles by simply clicking them.
ent-a-u14-shotgun-shell-loading-rig-u-p-p = Type 42 pattern shotgun shell loading rig
ent-a-u14-shotgun-shell-loading-rig-u-p-p-desc = An ammunition belt designed to hold shotgun shells, primarily for the Type 23 shotgun. # or individual bullets. TODO RMC14
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-u-p-p = Type 41 pattern lifesaver bag
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-u-p-p-desc = The Type 41 load rig is the standard load-bearing equipment of the UPP military. This configuration mounts a duffel bag filled with a range of injectors and light medical supplies, and is common among medics.
ent-a-u14-belt-smart-gun-operator-u-p-p = Type 90 pattern machinegunner belt
ent-a-u14-belt-smart-gun-operator-u-p-p-desc = Recently adopted by UPP military, this belt allows machinegunners to carry more ammo boxes into battle. It also found use with SOF breachers using Type 23 shotguns.
ent-a-u14-belt-smart-gun-operator-pistol-u-p-p = Type 92 pattern machinegunner sidearm rig
ent-a-u14-belt-smart-gun-operator-pistol-u-p-p-desc = Type 92 is an experimental ammo-carrying rig issued to UPP machinegunners which combines a sidearm holster with box-shaped pouches for limited storage.
ent-a-u14-belt-holster-pistol-u-p-p = Type 47 pistol holster rig
ent-a-u14-belt-holster-pistol-u-p-p-desc = This UPP-designed sidearm rig can very snugly and securely fit a Type-73, NP92, or a ZHNK-72, and their magazines or speedloaders. However, it lacks versatility in stored weaponry.
ent-a-u14-gloves-c-b-r-n-u-p-p = UPP MOPP gloves
ent-a-u14-gloves-c-b-r-n-u-p-p-desc = Part of the UPP's MOPP suit.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-boonie = UPP boonie
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-boonie-desc = UPP headgear issued to soldiers when they're not expected to face combat, and may be requested by officers and above.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-patrol-cap = UPP UL2 patrol cap
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-patrol-cap-desc = UPP headgear issued to soldiers when they're not expected to face combat, and may be requested by officers and above.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-ushanka = UPP UL8 ushanka
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-ushanka-desc = UPP headgear issued to soldiers when they're not expected to face combat, and may be requested by officers and above.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-c-b-r-n-hood = UPP MOPP hood
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-c-b-r-n-hood-desc = Hood from the UPP's Armed Forces MOPP costume.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-armor = UM5 personal armor
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-armor-desc = A set of Union of Progressive Peoples armor.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-armor-minimalistic = UL6 personal armor
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-armor-minimalistic-desc = A set of Minimalistic Union of Progressive Peoples armor. This pair is quite small compared to the standard, and will provide less protection.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-armor-bulky = UH7 heavy plated armor
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-armor-bulky-desc = A set of quite bulky Union of Progressive Peoples armor.
ent-a-u14-armor-smart-gun-desert-combat-harness-u-p-p = RVS-37 armoured automated machinegun harness
ent-a-u14-armor-smart-gun-desert-combat-harness-u-p-p-desc = Harness harness specially made for RVS-37 automated machinegun.
ent-a-u14-armor-army-u-p-p = 6B80 personal armor
ent-a-u14-armor-army-u-p-p-desc = An older UPP personal armor system that's since been replaced by the UPP Army Standard 6B90 body armor. It is still used by certain UPP Army units that the UPP doesn't expect to see much combat.
ent-a-u14-coat-u-p-p = UL4 officer jacket
ent-a-u14-coat-u-p-p-desc = A lightweight jacket, issued to officers of the UPP's military. Slightly protective from incoming damage, best off with proper armor however.
ent-a-u14-coat-u-p-p-senior = UL4 senior officer jacket
ent-a-u14-coat-u-p-p-senior-desc = A lightweight jacket, issued to senior officers of the UPP's military. Made of high-quality materials, even going as far as having the ranks and insignia of the Kapitan and their Company emblazoned on the shoulders and front of the jacket. Slightly protective from incoming damage, best off with proper armor however.
ent-a-u14-coat-u-p-p-m-p = UL4 camouflaged jacket
ent-a-u14-coat-u-p-p-m-p-desc = A lightweight jacket, issued to troops when they're not expected to engage in combat. Still studded to the brim with kevlar shards, though the synthread construction reduces its effectiveness.
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-naval-infantry-helmet = UPP Naval Infantry Helmet
ent-a-u14-u-p-p-naval-infantry-helmet-desc = A UPP Naval Infantry helmet.
ent-a-u14-armor-helmet-army-u-p-p = 6B82 combat helmet
ent-a-u14-armor-helmet-army-u-p-p-desc = An older version of the UPP Army's 6B92 combat helmet, still worn by certain units on planets the UPP deems less important.
ent-a-u14-altyn = Altyn-R2M
ent-a-u14-altyn-desc = An old earth design initially created for special forces and internal security to use in close quarters combat. Still worn by UPP forces after more than a century.
ent-a-u14-action-toggle-altyn-visor = Toggle the visor
ent-a-u14-action-toggle-altyn-visor-desc = Change the positions of the visor on your helmet.
ent-a-u14-fatigues-u-p-p = UPP naval infantry fatigues
ent-a-u14-fatigues-u-p-p-desc = A standard set of Union of Progressive Peoples Fatigues. It has shards of light Kevlar to help protect against shrapnel.
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-engi-u-p-p = UPP engineer fatigues
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-m-p-u-p-p = UPP military police fatigues
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-medic-u-p-p = UPP medic fatigues
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-officer-u-p-p = UPP officer fatigues
ent-a-u14-service-fatigues-u-p-p = UPP service uniform
ent-a-u14-service-fatigues-u-p-p-desc = Standart-issue UPP Army service uniform. Usually worn by officers.
ent-a-u14-boiler-fatigues-u-p-p = UPP boiler jumpsuit
ent-a-u14-boiler-fatigues-u-p-p-desc = Standart-issue UPP Army service uniform. Usually worn by pilots and aircrews.
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-army-u-p-p = UPP army fatigues
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-army-u-p-p-desc = A set of UPP fatigues, mass produced for the Armed Collective of the Union of Progressive Peoples. A rare sight, especially in 3WE zones. This particular set sports the standard UPP pattern of the UPP Army's 202nd Infantry Regiment.
ent-a-u14-suit-c-b-r-n-u-p-p = UPP MOPP suit
ent-a-u14-suit-c-b-r-n-u-p-p-desc = Jumpsuit from the UPP's Armed Forces MOPP suit.
ent-a-u14-joe-u-p-p = android suit
ent-a-u14-joe-u-p-p-desc = Uniform designed for UPP security synthetics.
ent-a-u14-glasses-smart-gun-sight-u-p-p = RVS-37 head rig
ent-a-u14-glasses-smart-gun-sight-u-p-p-desc = Developed for use with the RFVS-37, the Integrated Auto-Rifleman Optronic Device enables the riflemen of the UPP SOF to visually search for targets in low-visibility conditions, while also enabling safe use of the weapon itself.
ent-a-u14-webbing-drop-pouch-u-p-p = UPP marine drop pouch
ent-a-u14-webbing-drop-pouch-u-p-p-desc = A convenient pouch to carry loose items around.
ent-a-u14-webbing-admin-pouch-u-p-p = UPP marine admin pouch
ent-a-u14-webbing-admin-pouch-u-p-p-desc = A pouch to carry your administrative equipment around.
ent-a-u14-satchel-demo-spec-u-p-p = UPP rocket bag
ent-a-u14-satchel-demo-spec-u-p-p-desc = A specially-designed backpack for RPG users. It's made of two easily-accessible, waterproofed reinforced tubes and one smaller satchel slung at the bottom. The two silos are for rockets, but no one is stopping you from cramming other things in there.
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-shin-guards-u-p-p = UM5 shin guards
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-shin-guards-u-p-p-desc = An armor piece made to be used in combination with kestrel pattern armor.
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-shoulder-pads-u-p-p = UM5 shoulder pads
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-shoulder-pads-u-p-p-desc = An armor piece made to be used in combination with kestrel pattern armor.
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-crotch-pad-u-p-p = UM5 crotch pad
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-crotch-pad-u-p-p-desc = An armor piece made to be used in combination with kestrel pattern armor.
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-magazine-webbing-u-p-p = Type 41 pattern magazine webbing
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-magazine-webbing-u-p-p-desc = A magazine webbing made to be attached to the outside of personal armor.
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-large-webbing-u-p-p = Type 41 pattern large webbing
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-large-webbing-u-p-p-desc = A large webbing made to be attached to the outside of personal armor.
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-small-webbing-u-p-p = Type 41 pattern small webbing
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-small-webbing-u-p-p-desc = A small webbing made to be attached to the outside of personal armor.
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-jungle-poncho-u-p-p = Type 41 jungle rain poncho
ent-a-u14-armor-garb-jungle-poncho-u-p-p-desc = A poncho made to be used in combination with personal armor.
ent-a-u14-boots-c-b-r-n-u-p-p = UPP MOPP boots
ent-a-u14-boots-c-b-r-n-u-p-p-desc = Part of the UPP's MOPP suit.
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-deputy-windbreaker = CMB Deputy Windbreaker
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-deputy-windbreaker-desc = A windbreaker made for CMB deputies.
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-marshal-windbreaker = CMB Marshal Windbreaker
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-marshal-windbreaker-desc = A windbreaker made for CMB marshals.
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-c-i-u-armor = CMB CIU Armor
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-c-i-u-armor-desc = A set of CMB Crisis Intervention Unit armor.
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-c-i-u-helmet = CMB CIU Helmet
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-c-i-u-helmet-desc = A CMB Crisis Intervention Unit riot helmet.
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-uniform = CMB Uniform
ent-a-u14-c-m-b-uniform-desc = The uniform of the Colonial Marshal Bureau.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-ball-cap = WY PMC Ball Cap
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-ball-cap-desc = A WY PMC patrol cap.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-p-o-cap = WY PPO Ball Cap
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-p-o-cap-desc = A WY Personal Protection Officer cap.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-armor = WY PMC Armor
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-armor-desc = A set of Weyland-Yutani PMC armor.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-armor-min = WY PMC Minimalistic Armor
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-armor-min-desc = A set of Weyland-Yutani PMC armor. This pair is quite small compared to the standard, and will provide less protection.
ent-a-u14-suit-bio-we-yu = WeYu-TSS MK I - bio suit
ent-a-u14-suit-bio-we-yu-desc = The 'Weyland-Yutani TerraScientia bio-suit MK I'. An advanced light-weight bio-suit developed in-house by Weyland-Yutani. It's a suit that protects against biological contamination.
ent-c-m-u-suit-bio-w-y-sec = armored WeYu-TSS MK I - bio suit
ent-c-m-u-suit-bio-w-y-sec-desc = The 'Weyland-Yutani TerraScientia bio-suit MK I'. An advanced light-weight bio-suit developed in-house by Weyland-Yutani. It's a suit that protects against biological contamination. This one has been fitted with an armored vest.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-armor-engineer = WY PMC Engineer Armor
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-armor-engineer-desc = A set of Weyland-Yutani PMC Engineer armor.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-p-o-armor = WY PPO Armor
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-p-o-armor-desc = A set of Weyland-Yutani Personal Protection Officer armor. This pair is quite small compared to the standard, and will provide less protection.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-helmet = WY PMC Helmet
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-helmet-desc = A WY PMC helmet.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-sniper-hat = WY PMC Sniper Hat
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-sniper-hat-desc = A WY PMC helmet.
ent-a-u14-armor-helmet-p-m-c-tactical = WY PMC Tactical Helmet
ent-a-u14-armor-helmet-p-m-c-tactical-desc = A contender for service with the Royal Marines Commandos, it is presently, exclusively, field tested by Weyland-Yutani mercenaries. Features a ballistic mask and integrated display connected to the visor.
ent-a-u14-armor-helmet-p-m-c-tactical-engi = WY PMC Tactical Engineer Helmet
ent-a-u14-armor-helmet-p-m-c-tactical-engi-desc = A contender for service with the Royal Marines Commandos, it is presently, exclusively, field tested by Weyland-Yutani mercenaries. Features a ballistic mask and integrated display connected to the visor.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-helmet-heavy = WY PMC Heavy Helmet
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-helmet-heavy-desc = A WY PMC helmet.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-fatigues = WY PMC Fatigues
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-fatigues-desc = A standard set of Weyland-Yutani PMC Fatigues. It has shards of light Kevlar to help protect against shrapnel.
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-veteran-p-m-c-corporate = We-Yu corporate security uniform
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-veteran-p-m-c-corporate-desc = An armored uniform worn by We-Yu corporate security members. This variant is commonly worn by what are known as 'goons'.
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-veteran-p-m-c-corporate-lead = We-Yu corporate security uniform
ent-a-u14-jumpsuit-veteran-p-m-c-corporate-lead-desc = An armored uniform worn by We-Yu corporate security members. This variant is commonly worn by the lead of the 'goonsquad', as they are colloquially known.
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-fatigues-engineer = WY PMC Engineer Fatigues
ent-a-u14-w-y-p-m-c-fatigues-engineer-desc = A standard set of Weyland-Yutani PMC Engineer Fatigues. It has shards of light Kevlar to help protect against shrapnel.
ent-a-u14-w-y-guard-fatigues = WY Guard Fatigues
ent-a-u14-w-y-guard-fatigues-desc = A standard set of Weyland-Yutani Guard Fatigues. It has shards of light Kevlar to help protect against shrapnel.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-boots = LACN Boots
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-boots-desc = Standard issue LACN boots.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-gloves = LACN combat gloves
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-gloves-desc = Standard issue LACN combat gloves with insulated fibers.
ent-a-u14-mask-l-a-c-n-pilot-oxygen = LACN LAH-99 Oxygen Mask
ent-a-u14-mask-l-a-c-n-pilot-oxygen-desc = A mask attached to LACN LAH-99 helmets to provide aircrew with breathable oxygen.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-navy-cap = LACN Cap
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-navy-cap-desc = A standard cap made for the LACN.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-beanie = LACN Commandos Beanie
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-beanie-desc = A beanie used by the Naval Commandos of the LACN.
ent-a-u14-u-s-a-s-f-s-e-c-f-o-r-beret = USASF Security Forces Beret
ent-a-u14-u-s-a-s-f-s-e-c-f-o-r-beret-desc = A beret bearing the insignia of the USASF Security Forces.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-armor-standard = LACN BL-1 Armor
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-armor-standard-desc = A set of ballistic armor used by the LACN landing forces.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-armor-standard-padless = Padless LACN BL-1 Armor
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-armor-standard-padless-desc = A set of ballistic armor used by the LACN landing forces. This one is missing the grieves and shoulder pads.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-armor-s-l = LACN BL-2 Armor
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-armor-s-l-desc = A set of ballistic armor used by the LACN landing forces NCOs and Officers.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-armor-standard = LACN BL-4L Armor
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-armor-standard-desc = A set of ballistic armor used by the LACN naval commandos.
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-flak-vest = CLF flak vest
ent-a-u14-c-l-f-flak-vest-desc = An imported flak vest that comes from your foreign buyer in the UPP. You have no idea the origin of it.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-armor-scout = LACN BL-4L Scout Armor
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-armor-scout-desc = A set of ballistic armor used by the LACN naval commando scouts.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-armor-pointman = LACN BL-4L Pointman Armor
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-commando-armor-pointman-desc = A set of ballistic armor used by the LACN naval commando pointmen.
ent-a-u14-u-s-a-s-f-s-e-c-f-o-r-chestrig = USASF Security Forces Chestrig
ent-a-u14-u-s-a-s-f-s-e-c-f-o-r-chestrig-desc = An exterior chestrig used by USASF SECFOR.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-i-c-p-s2 = LACN ICPS-2 Aircrew Armor
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-i-c-p-s2-desc = A set of ballistic armor used by LACN aircrew with an attached oxygen tank.
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-c-n-l-a-h99-visor-mirror = Orange LAH-99 Visor
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-c-n-l-a-h99-visor-mirror-desc = A visor attached to LACN LAH-99 helmets, this one is reflective. This item must be attached to a LAH-99 helmet.
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-c-n-l-a-h99-visor = Transparent Orange LAH-99 Visor
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-c-n-l-a-h99-visor-desc = A visor attached to LAH-99 helmets. This item must be attached to a LAH-99 helmet.
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-h99-visor-high-tech = IHADSS LAH-99 Visor
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-h99-visor-high-tech-desc = An Integrated Helmet and Display Sighting System attached to LAH-99 helmets. This item must be attached to a LAH-99 helmet.
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-c-n-l-a-h99-visor-clear = Transparent LAH-99 Visor
ent-a-u14-goggles-l-a-c-n-l-a-h99-visor-clear-desc = A visor attached to LAH-99 helmets. This item must be attached to a LAH-99 helmet.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-helmet-standard = LACN BK-9 Helmet
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-helmet-standard-desc = Standard Issue Helmet used by LACN landing forces. Provides modest protection from bullets and melee attacks at the head.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-helmet-s-l = LACN BK-9M Helmet
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-helmet-s-l-desc = A slightly more modern helmet made for LACN landing forces NCOs and Officers. This one contains a small built-in camera and has cushioning to protect your fragile brain.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-air-crew-helmet = LACN LAH-99 aircrew helmet
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-air-crew-helmet-desc = A helmet made for LACN aircrew. This one contains a small built-in camera and has cushioning to protect your fragile brain.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-uniform = LACN Fatigues
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-uniform-desc = Standard-issue LACN landing forces fatigues. They have shards of light Kevlar to help protect against stabbing weapons and bullets.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-uniform-coat = Cold Weather LACN Fatigues
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-uniform-coat-desc = Standard-issue LACN landing forces fatigues with a warm overcoat. They have shards of light Kevlar to help protect against stabbing weapons and bullets.
ent-a-u14-u-s-a-s-f-sec-for-uniform = USASF Security Forces Fatigues
ent-a-u14-u-s-a-s-f-sec-for-uniform-desc = Standard-issue USASF SECFOR fatigues. They have shards of light Kevlar to help protect against stabbing weapons and bullets.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-pilot-jumpsuit = LACN Aircrew Jumpsuit
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-pilot-jumpsuit-desc = A standard LACN Aircrew Jumpsuit. It has shards of light Kevlar to help protect against shrapnel.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-backpack = LACN standardweight backpack
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-backpack-desc = The standard-issue pack of LACN landing forces. Designed to lug gear into the battlefield.
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-ammo-backpack = LACN ammo bearer backpack
ent-a-u14-l-a-c-n-ammo-backpack-desc = The standard-issue pack of LACN landing forces with an extra ammo can attached to it. Designed to lug gear into the battlefield.
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-cap = CWPS Ball Cap
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-cap-desc = A simple ball cap with the logo of the Colonial Wilderness Preservation Service.
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-campaign-hat = CWPS Campaign Hat
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-campaign-hat-desc = A wide brimed hat used by the rangers of the Colonial Wilderness Preservation Service.
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-bomber = CWPS Bomber Jacket
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-bomber-desc = A bomber jacket used by the rangers of the Colonial Wilderness Preservation Service.
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-uniform = CWPS Uniform
ent-a-u14-c-w-p-s-uniform-desc = The standard uniform of the Colonial Wilderness Preservation Service rangers.
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-combat-prodigy-r-u = L177 Prodigy pattern combat toolbelt rig
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-combat-prodigy-r-u-desc = Standart-issue Royal Marines Commando rig of the Prodigy Armed Repair Teams for Response Units conducting repairs within combat zones. It consists of a modular belt with various clips and pouches for tools along with a holster for a sidearm. Due to the bulk of the sidearm and one magazine.
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-prodigy = PSC-TM626 pattern medical bag
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-prodigy-desc = The PSC-TM626 is the standard load-bearing equipment of the Prodigy security forces. This configuration mounts a duffel bag filled with a range of injectors and light medical supplies, and is common among medics, sources say its just a W-Y TM625 bag, but Prodigy denies this claim.
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-prodigy-filled = PSC-TM626 pattern medical bag
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-prodigy-filled-desc = The PSC-TM626 is the standard load-bearing equipment of the Prodigy security forces. This configuration mounts a duffel bag filled with a range of injectors and light medical supplies, and is common among medics, sources say its just a W-Y TM625 bag, but Prodigy denies this claim.
ent-a-u14-visor-night-vision-prodigy = prodigy night vision optic
ent-a-u14-visor-night-vision-prodigy-desc = An insertable visor HUD into a standard Prodigy helmet. This type gives a form of night vision and is standard issue in units with regular funding. It can be inserted into a recharger to recharge its internal battery.
ent-r-m-c-satchel-welder-r-u = Prodigy response unit technician welderpack
ent-r-m-c-satchel-welder-r-u-desc = Ergonomic, protected, high capacity backpack, designed for Prodigy Armed Repair Teams. Features a small fueltank for quick blowtorch refueling.
ent-r-m-c-satchel-welder-r-u-cloak = Prodigy response unit technician welder stealth pack
ent-r-m-c-satchel-welder-r-u-cloak-desc = Ergonomic, protected, high capacity backpack, designed for Prodigy Armed Repair Teams. Features a small fueltank for quick blowtorch refueling. Also has a cloaking module for synthetic units
ent-a-u14-pouch-medical-prodigy = Prodigy tactical medical pouch
ent-a-u14-pouch-medical-prodigy-desc = A heavy pouch containing everything one needs to get themselves back on their feet. Quite the selection.
ent-a-u14-pouch-medical-prodigy-filled = Prodigy tactical medical pouch
ent-a-u14-pouch-medical-prodigy-filled-desc = A heavy pouch containing everything one needs to get themselves back on their feet. Quite the selection.
ent-a-u14-pouch-magazine-large-p-a-r-t-dual = Prodigy dual large magazine pouch
ent-a-u14-pouch-magazine-large-p-a-r-t-dual-desc = A large pouch designed to hold four large magazines, and 4 handfulls of shotgun shells. The pouch is designed for the Prodigy Armed Repair Teams, and is often used by their engineers and medics to hold extra magazines and shotgun shells.
ent-a-u14-pouch-magazine-large-p-a-r-t-dual-filled = Prodigy dual large magazine pouch
ent-a-u14-pouch-magazine-large-p-a-r-t-dual-filled-desc = A large pouch designed to hold four large magazines, and 4 handfulls of shotgun shells. The pouch is designed for the Prodigy Armed Repair Teams, and is often used by their engineers and medics to hold extra magazines and shotgun shells.
ent-a-u14-pouch-i-f-a-k-prodigy = Prodigy first-aid pouch
ent-a-u14-hands-prodigy-r-u = Prodigy Response Unit gloves
ent-a-u14-hands-prodigy-r-u-desc = Standard issue kevlon fiber gloves manufactured for and by Prodigy Security Corp. They are insulated against electrical shock.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-cap = Prodigy Security Forces Cap
ent-a-u14-prodigy-cap-desc = A simple patrol cap with the logo of the Prodigy Corporation on the front.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-beret = Prodigy Security Forces Beret
ent-a-u14-prodigy-beret-desc = A beret used by command members of the Prodigy Corporation.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-beret-p-a-r-t = Prodigy Armed Repair Team Command Beret
ent-a-u14-prodigy-beret-p-a-r-t-desc = A beret used by command members of the Prodigy Armed Repair Team, the elite forces of Prodigy Security Corp. The beret is a symbol of their status and is only given to those who have proven themselves in combat and repair situations. The beret is adorned with the Prodigy logo and is a source of pride for those who wear it.
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-cap-grey = prodigy cap
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-cap-grey-desc = A grey cap with Prodigy CORP logo on its front. Has some ventilation holes as well.
ent-c-m-u-armor-prodigy-flak-vest-desc = A light flak vest.
ent-c-m-u-armor-prodigy-flak-vest = flak webbing vest
ent-c-m-u-armor-prodigy-flak-vest-alt-desc = A light flak vest.
ent-c-m-u-armor-prodigy-flak-vest-alt = flak vest
ent-c-m-u-armor-prodigy-flak-vest-medical-desc = A light flak vest.
ent-c-m-u-armor-prodigy-flak-vest-medical = medical flak vest
ent-a-u14-armor-prodigy-x-a-s23 = PRU-XAS-23 pattern battle armor
ent-a-u14-armor-prodigy-x-a-s23-desc = Tougher than steel, quieter than whispers, the PRU-XAS-23 Pattern Battle Armor provides capable protection combined with an experimental integrated motion tracker. It took an R&D team a weekend to develop and costs more than the Romulus Station... probably. When worn, uniform accessories such as webbing cannot be attached due to the motion sensors occupying the clips, although the expanded storage on the physical armor makes up for it. Due to its awkardness it requires the clips on the Prodigy Response Unit uniform to wear.
ent-a-u14-armor-prodigy-x-a-s23-g = PRU-XAS-23-G pattern battle armor
ent-a-u14-armor-prodigy-x-a-s23-g-desc = Tougher than steel, quieter than whispers, the PRU-XAS-23-G Pattern Battle Armor provides capable protection for smart gunners, ditching the built in motion detector for SG rigs. When worn, uniform accessories such as webbing cannot be attached due to the gunner rig occupying the clips, although the expanded storage on the physical armor makes up for it. Due to its awkwardness and increased armor from the normal model it requires the clips on the Prodigy Response Unit uniform to wear.
ent-a-u14-armor-prodigy-x-a-s23-s = PRU-XAS-23-S pattern battle armor
ent-a-u14-armor-prodigy-x-a-s23-s-desc = Tougher than kevlar, quieter than whispers, the PRU-XAS-23-S Pattern Battle Armor provides capable protection for synthetics, combined with an experimental integrated motion trackers. When worn, uniform accessories such as webbing cannot be attached due to the motion detector occupying the clips, although the expanded storage on the physical armor makes up for it. Due to its awkwardness and lighter armor from the normal model it requires the clips on the Prodigy Response Unit uniform to wear.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-ballistic-helmet = ballistic helmet
ent-a-u14-prodigy-ballistic-helmet-desc = A cheaply produced ballistic helmet used by the Prodigy Corporation.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-ballistic-helmet-p-a-r-t = PART ballistic helmet
ent-a-u14-prodigy-ballistic-helmet-p-a-r-t-desc = A more robust ballistic helmet used by PART operatives.
ent-a-u14-p-a-r-t-operator-helmet-heavy = PART Gunner Operator Ballistic Helmet
ent-a-u14-p-a-r-t-operator-helmet-heavy-desc = A heavy ballistic helmet with mask for PART Heavy gunners, the orange tint on the eye holes protect from bullet flashes and sun glare to allow continous firing.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-fatigues = prodigy fatigues
ent-a-u14-prodigy-fatigues-desc = Standard-issue Prodigy Security Forces fatigues.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-fatigues-r-u = Prodigy Armed Repair Team specialized fatigues
ent-a-u14-prodigy-fatigues-r-u-desc = Standard-issue Prodigy Armed Repair Team fatigues. The PART-SF is a specialized uniform designed for Prodigy Security Corp's Armed Repair Teams, who are responsible for maintaining and repairing equipment in high-risk environments. The uniform features reinforced padding on the knees and elbows, as well as multiple pockets for carrying tools and supplies. It also includes a built-in harness system for attaching additional gear and equipment.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-fatigues-r-u-synth = Prodigy Armed Repair Team Synthetic fatigues
ent-a-u14-prodigy-fatigues-r-u-synth-desc = Standard-issue Prodigy Armed Repair Team fatigues for Synthetics. The PART-SF is a specialized uniform designed for Prodigy Security Corp's Armed Repair Teams, who are responsible for maintaining and repairing equipment in high-risk environments. The uniform features reinforced padding on the knees and elbows, as well as multiple pockets for carrying tools and supplies. It also includes a built-in harness system for attaching additional gear and equipment.
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-black-skirt = black skirt suit
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-black-skirt-desc = An elegant black suit with a skirt and a white shirt. Made with high-class fabric, it is perfect for careerists or girl bossing. Its size fits everyone with enough confidence. The label says "PRODIGY CORP. 100% WOOL. DRY CLEAN ONLY. DO NOT WASH. DESIGNED IN NEW SIAM". Weirdly enough, there's no information on where it was produced.
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-grey-skirt = grey skirt suit
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-grey-skirt-desc = An elegant grey suit with a skirt and a white shirt. Made with high-class fabric, it is perfect for careerists or girl bossing. Its size fits everyone with enough confidence. The label says "PRODIGY CORP. 100% WOOL. DRY CLEAN ONLY. DO NOT WASH. DESIGNED IN NEW SIAM". Weirdly enough, there's no information on where it was produced.
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-black = black suit
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-black-desc = An elegant black suit and white shirt. Made with high-class fabric, it is perfect for careerists or being arrogant douchebag. Its size fits everyone with enough confidence. The label says "PRODIGY CORP. 100% WOOL. DRY CLEAN ONLY. DO NOT WASH. DESIGNED IN NEW SIAM". Weirdly enough, there's no information on where it was produced.
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-grey = grey suit
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-suit-grey-desc = An elegant grey suit and white shirt. Made with high-class fabric, it is perfect for careerists or being arrogant douchebag. Its size fits everyone with enough confidence. The label says "PRODIGY CORP. 100% WOOL. DRY CLEAN ONLY. DO NOT WASH. DESIGNED IN NEW SIAM". Weirdly enough, there's no information on where it was produced.
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-jumpsuit-grey = grey jumpsuit
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-jumpsuit-grey-desc = Grey working one-piece boilersuit. Looks like a solid piece of gear, made out of ripstop fabric. The label says "PRODIGY CORP. RIPSTOP. FR. IS. AS. DO NOT BLEACH.". Has quite a few pockets, though some of them are for design purposes only.
ent-a-u14-prodigy-laptop = Prodigy Advanced Systems Tampering System (PASTS)
ent-a-u14-prodigy-laptop-desc = A ruggedized military laptop used for remote control and programming made by Prodigy Security Corp. Can be placed on tables for easier access. Works as a sentry laptop as well!
ent-a-u14-extraction-team-beacon = Prodigy Extraction Team Beacon
ent-a-u14-extraction-team-beacon-desc = A disposable uplink used to call the Prodigy extraction team. It's useless after activation. What do you mean its just an expensive laser pointer? (OOC Note, if this fails to work please ahelp and ask them to spawn ProdigyExtractionParty)
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-lawyer-beacon = prodigy lawyer beacon
ent-c-m-u14-prodigy-lawyer-beacon-desc = A disposable uplink used to call the Prodigy lawyer. It's useless after activation. What do you mean its just an expensive laser pointer? (OOC Note, if this fails to work please ahelp and ask them to spawn ProdigyLawyer)
ent-a-u14-synth-reset-key-prodigy = Prodigy synthetic reset key
ent-a-u14-synth-reset-key-prodigy-desc = A Prodigy-pattern reset key for rebooting synthetic units after critical failure. It must be recharged after use.
ent-a-u14-belt-marine-r-m-c = L70 pattern ammo load rig
ent-a-u14-belt-marine-r-m-c-desc = Standart-issue Royal Marines Commando rig. It consists of a modular belt with various clips. This is the standard variant, designed for bulk ammunition-carrying operations.
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-general-r-m-c = L26 general utility pouch
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-general-r-m-c-desc = A small, lightweight pouch that can be clipped onto kestrel armour to provide additional storage. The newer model, while uncomfortable, can also be clipped around the waist.
ent-a-u14-belt-medical-r-m-c = L75 pattern medical storage rig
ent-a-u14-belt-medical-r-m-c-desc = Standart-issue Royal Marines Commando rig. It consists of a modular belt with various clips. This version is a less common configuration, designed to transport bulkier medical supplies.
ent-a-u14-belt-holster-pistol-r-m-c = L165 pattern general pistol holster rig
ent-a-u14-belt-holster-pistol-r-m-c-desc = Standart-issue Royal Marines Commando rig. It consists of a modular belt with various clips. This version has a holster assembly that allows one to carry the most common pistols. It also contains side pouches that can store most pistol magazines.
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-combat-r-m-c = L177 pattern combat toolbelt rig
ent-a-u14-belt-utility-combat-r-m-c-desc = Standart-issue Royal Marines Commando rig of the RMC for engineers conducting repairs within combat zones. It consists of a modular belt with various clips and pouches for tools along with a holster for a sidearm. Due to the bulk of the sidearm, it is unable to hold as many tools as its standard counterpart.
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-r-m-c = L75 pattern lifesaver bag
ent-a-u14-belt-medic-bag-r-m-c-desc = Standart-issue Royal Marines Commando rig. This configuration mounts a duffel bag filled with a range of injectors and light medical supplies, and is common among medics.
ent-a-u14-shotgun-shell-loading-rig-r-m-c = L70 pattern shotgun shell loading rig
ent-a-u14-shotgun-shell-loading-rig-r-m-c-desc = An ammunition belt designed to hold shotgun shells. # or individual bullets. TODO RMC14
ent-a-u14-belt-mortar-grenadier-r-m-c = L84 pattern ammo load rig
ent-a-u14-belt-mortar-grenadier-r-m-c-desc = An L84 pattern load-bearing rig configured to carry support ammunition for either the L53A1 light mortar or L164A3 multiple grenade launcher, along with a sidearm & magazine. Made of special rot-resistant fabric.
ent-a-u14-hands-r-m-c = L6 pattern combat gloves
ent-a-u14-hands-r-m-c-desc = Standard issue tactical gloves used by the Royal Marines Commando.
ent-a-u14-hands-silver-r-m-c = L6 pattern silver combat gloves
ent-a-u14-mask-gas-r-m-c = L7 pattern gasmask
ent-a-u14-mask-gas-r-m-c-desc = The standard issue gasmask utilized by the TWE Royal Marines Commandos and IASF.
ent-a-u14-mask-prescription-gas-r-m-c = prescription L7 pattern gasmask
ent-a-u14-mask-prescription-gas-r-m-c-desc = The standard issue gasmask utilized by the TWE Royal Marines Commandos and IASF. Contains prescription lenses.
ent-a-u14-head-turban-r-m-c = royal marine turban
ent-a-u14-head-turban-r-m-c-desc = A standard military turban found in the Three World Empire Royal Marines Commando. Considered a rare item, these kind of turbans are prized by collectors.
ent-a-u14-head-beret-r-m-c = royal marine beret
ent-a-u14-head-beret-r-m-c-desc = A green beret belonging to the Three World Empire Royal Marines Commando.
ent-a-u14-head-beret-r-m-c-lead = royal marine sergeant beret
ent-a-u14-head-beret-r-m-c-lead-desc = A green beret belonging to the Three World Empire Royal Marines Commando.
ent-a-u14-head-beret-r-m-c-officer = royal marine officer beret
