ent-a-u14-black-box-recorder = colony blackbox recorder
ent-a-u14-black-box-recorder-desc = An ICC mandated data recorder installed in all UA, UPP and TWE registered colonies. Engineered to survive catastrophic events, it continuously logs critical environmental, structural and operational data. In the event of a disaster, it enables investigators to reconstruct the sequence of events and determine the root cause of failure. This one however, is not red.
ent-a-u14-watch-tower1 = Watch Tower
ent-a-u14-watch-tower1-desc = A Watch Tower.
ent-a-u14-hesco-kit = HESCO kit
ent-a-u14-hesco-kit-desc = A collapsible wire-mesh basket. Deploy it on the ground facing the direction you want it to face, then pack it with dirt using an entrenching tool.
ent-a-u14-hesco-unfilled1 = unfilled HESCO basket
ent-a-u14-hesco-unfilled1-desc = An empty wire-mesh HESCO basket. It needs to be packed with dirt before it will do much of anything.
ent-a-u14-hesco-unfilled2 = partially filled HESCO basket
ent-a-u14-hesco-unfilled2-desc = A HESCO basket half-filled with dirt. It needs more before it becomes useful cover.
ent-a-u14-hesco-unfilled3 = mostly filled HESCO basket
ent-a-u14-hesco-unfilled3-desc = A HESCO basket mostly filled with dirt. Almost ready to serve as cover.
ent-a-u14-hesco-short-complete = HESCO barricade
ent-a-u14-hesco-short-complete-desc = A sand-filled HESCO basket. Sturdy cover, though still low enough to vault over. It can still be extended higher to become a wall.
ent-a-u14-hesco-tall-building1 = raised HESCO basket
ent-a-u14-hesco-tall-building1-desc = The HESCO basket has been raised higher, but still needs to be packed with more dirt before it will stop bullets or sightlines.
