ent-a-u14-guidebook-law-colonial = colonial civil code
ent-a-u14-guidebook-law-colonial-desc = A thick, well-thumbed but battered volume bearing the seal of the Orbital Court and the Colonial Administration. The historical first-edition of the Colonial Civil Code, printed long before the latest reforms. Its pages are considered dated being full of precedents that modern jurists dispute with dubious legal reasoning and clauses that have never been updated. No two lawyers can agree on what half of it actually means, still, every colonial office seems to have one, and it remains in circulation as a reminder that law is a living thing. It is affectionately called: 'The Blue Book'.
ent-a-u14-briefcase-law-bundle = counselor's law bundle
ent-a-u14-briefcase-law-bundle-desc = A sturdy brown briefcase containing the complete legal library of the colony: the Colonial Civil Code (the Blue Book), the UCMJ (the Devil's Red Book), the SOP, and bureaucratic legal weaponry. Lawyers call it the 'Counselor's Burden', everybody else just calls it the briefcase full of trouble. Everything a budding legal mind needs to ruin someone's day with a technicality.
ent-a-u14-sentry-omni-we-yu = WY 571-D omnidirectional sentry gun
ent-a-u14-sentry-omni-we-yu-desc = A Weyland-Yutani-configured 571-D sentry gun. Its locked corporate IFF recognizes Weyland-Yutani personnel, security, synthetics, contractors, and private military forces.
ent-a-u14-turret-almayer-we-yu = WY UA-635C static gauss turret
ent-a-u14-turret-almayer-we-yu-desc = A Weyland-Yutani-configured static gauss turret with a locked corporate IFF.
ent-a-u14-deployer-sentry-we-yu = WY sentry deployment system
ent-a-u14-deployer-sentry-we-yu-desc = A Weyland-Yutani-configured deployment system containing a corporate-IFF static gauss turret.
ent-a-u14-bangalore = bangalore demolition charge
ent-a-u14-bangalore-desc = A demolition charge used to clear obstacles and breach fortifications. Once placed on the ground it arms itself and detonates after 20 seconds.
